.nh
.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-metrics - View system metrics from servers


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako metrics [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Display system metrics (CPU, memory, disk, load, network and disk I/O)
collected by takod on each server, plus OS update and reboot status.

.PP
takod samples host metrics natively every 60 seconds and keeps a bounded
on-node history (7 days by default). Without --since this command shows the
latest sample; --since shows min/avg/max/last and a sparkline per metric for
that window (for example --since 24h or --since 2026-10-11T00:00:00Z), with
--step choosing the bucket size.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for metrics

.PP
\fB--live\fP[=false]
	Continuous live updates

.PP
\fB--once\fP[=false]
	Collect metrics once immediately

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--server\fP=""
	Specific server to monitor

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	Show history for this window: a duration (24h, 7d) or an RFC3339 timestamp

.PP
\fB--step\fP=""
	History bucket size with --since (e.g. 5m; default picks at most 360 buckets)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to use (default: the only environment, else production, else the first alphabetically)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB--preview\fP=""
	preview environment to use (deploy, ps, logs, exec, history, rollback, config explain); -e then names its base

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako(1)\fP
